{
  "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
  "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 10-9646, Miller v. Alabama. Mr. Stevenson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What about 50 years? Is that -- is that too much?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bryan A. Stevenson, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEVENSON: I would hold that children are categorically prohibited from being subjected to sentences --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stevenson",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think one of the problems, Your Honor, with -- with trying to make these judgments is that -- that even psychologists say that we can't make good long-term judgments about the rehabilitation and transitory character of these young people. That's the reason why in Graham this Court didn't permit that kind of discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, if that's the criterion, is everything that you say irrelevant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John C. Neiman, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Imposing life without parole sentences on aggravated murder offenders like Evan Miller is in line with the national consensus, is morally justified, and is consistent with legitimate penological goals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JOHN C. NEIMAN, JR., ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Life without parole is the minimum?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Out of the 39 States or jurisdictions that allow this sentence, as Mr. Stevens has indicated -- or Mr. Stevenson has indicated, a good chunk of them, 27 in all, make the sentence the minimum sentence under the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are juries instructed that life without parole is a necessary consequence of their decision? I suppose a defense attorney could argue it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the -- in the Petitioner's briefs, the idea of deterrence kind of drops by the way side. Have there been any studies that show that there is a deterrence value?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Criminologists (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is an amicus brief submitted by criminologists in this case, and it looks specifically at the question of deterrence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are some studies that have established that juveniles are more likely or less likely to recidivate after an intervention than adults. Generally speaking, homicide offenders are categorically less likely to recidivate than many non-homicide offenders. Drug offenders and property crime offenders are much more likely to recidivate than -- than homicide offenders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Neiman",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Neiman has -- argued that we can read into these statutes a commitment to imposing life without parole at a particular age, and that age is the age of transfer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think the legislators in Pennsylvania and Michigan don't understand what their laws provide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stevenson",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I think that they haven't thought about it. Yes, I do think that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Then does the constitutional rule change?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stevenson",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think it changes, because there is an age at which this Court is obligated under the Eighth Amendment to say a sentence of this sort, a permanent judgment that life-long incarceration is -- is required --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if, instead of striking down the laws in these States, why don't we just require the State legislatures to think about it? All right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "981ed7c7c3d7bb166ea5949d5233cb7a64a02375211d22a0eabbd31a4cbc8c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-981ed7c7c3d7-0003-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "people who are vulnerable from excessive punishment. And this is a cohort that we contend is the most vulnerable and should be shielded from this excessive punishment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9646",
      "confidence": 0.0,
